WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.600
A mic on stage picks up the speaker.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:06.170
The sound loops back, builds, and then it howls.

3
00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.930
Today, engineers pull the fader down,

4
00:00:08.930 --> 00:00:10.970
or they notch out frequencies.

5
00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.860
That costs you volume.

6
00:00:13.010 --> 00:00:14.510
And it costs you tone.

7
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:19.070
Nullyn AI sits inline,
between the mic and the console.

8
00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.430
It listens to the mic, and to the speaker feed.

9
00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.670
It predicts the feedback path in real time,

10
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.100
and it takes the loop out before it rings.

11
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:31.130
So the voice and the instruments stay natural.

12
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:36.050
Version one runs on a laptop,
with a USB audio interface.

13
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:39.260
Version two is our own dedicated box.

14
00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.780
Version three deploys at scale.

15
00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:46.610
Nullyn AI. More gain before feedback,
without wrecking the sound.

16
00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.300
nullyn.ai
